.SH DESCRIPTION
.TP
\f[B]load_set\f[R](\f[I]path\f[R])
Read a question set from a file and return a \f[B]QuestionSet\f[R] (see
\f[B]jeopardy\-model\f[R](3)).
A file ending in \f[I].json\f[R] is parsed as JSON, any other as YAML.
Raises \f[B]LoadError\f[R] if the file cannot be read or parsed, does
not match the format, or fails \f[B]check\f[R].
The message starts with the path.
.TP
\f[B]check\f[R](\f[I]qs\f[R])
Run the semantic checks that the format alone cannot express and return
a list of error messages, empty if the set is fine.
The errors are: no categories, categories of different sizes, a category
without clues, values that are not ascending or not positive, or a clue
already marked answered.
.TP
\f[B]validate_main\f[R](\f[I]argv\f[R]=None)
Entry point of \f[B]jeopardy\-validate\f[R](1).
Prints one result per file, with a warning if the set has no final clue,
and exits the process with status 0 or 1.
Uses \f[B]sys.argv\f[R][1:] when \f[I]argv\f[R] is None.
.TP
\f[B]LoadError\f[R]
Exception raised by \f[B]load_set\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
from jeopardy.loader import load_set, LoadError

try:
    qs = load_set(\(dqgames/sample.yaml\(dq)
except LoadError as err:
    print(err)
